---
// Homepage section advertising the "Ask the book" assistant and walking the
// reader through the one-time setup. Primary path is one-click OAuth with
// OpenRouter (no key to copy or paste); pasting a key manually is the advanced
// fallback. Saves to the same localStorage the chapter chat reads (see
// ../scripts/assistant-config.ts), so once set up here the assistant is active
// on every chapter page.
---

<section class="home-assistant" id="assistant">
  <h2>Ask the Book, an AI study assistant on every page</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Ask the Book</strong> is an optional AI study assistant available throughout the book.
    If you prefer to read without it, simply skip this section and continue with the text.
    If enabled, the assistant can answer questions about the chapter you are reading,
    explain derivations, unpack notation, render mathematical expressions, and help
    connect ideas across the material. Its goal is to support understanding, not simply
    provide answers.
  </p>
  <p>
    There are two ways to use the assistant:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>1. Connect an AI provider.</strong><br>
    The quickest way to get started: connect a free
    <a href="https://openrouter.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenRouter</a> account
    with one click below. OpenRouter offers free access to a
    wide range of open-source models (and, optionally, paid access to frontier models such
    as Claude or GPT through the same account). You can also bring your own API key from
    OpenAI, Anthropic, or any other supported provider. The assistant will use the model you choose to answer your questions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>2. Run a model locally.</strong><br>
    If you have a compatible GPU, you can download and run an open-source language model
    directly on your own machine. This option offers complete privacy and does not require
    any account or API. Go to any chapter page and choose <strong>In your browser</strong> in the assistant's ⚙ settings.
  </p>

  <h3>Getting started (about a minute)</h3>
  <ol class="setup-steps">
    <li>
      <strong>New to OpenRouter?</strong>
      <a href="https://openrouter.ai/sign-up" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Create a free
      account</a> first (opens in a new tab; if it offers you an API key along the way,
      store it, but you won't need it for this setup), then come back to this page. Already have an account? Skip ahead.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pick a model and click <strong>Connect with OpenRouter</strong> below. You'll approve
      the connection on openrouter.ai with one click and be sent straight back here, ready
      to go. The connection creates a key scoped to this site, which you can view, limit,
      or revoke at any time from your
      <a href="https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenRouter dashboard</a>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="setup-form">
    <label class="setup-field">
      <span>Free model</span>
      <select id="sg-model"><option>Loading free models…</option></select>
    </label>
    <button id="sg-connect" type="button">Connect with OpenRouter</button>
    <p id="sg-status" class="setup-status" role="status"></p>

    <details class="setup-manual">
      <summary>Prefer to use your Claude, OpenAI, or other supported provider via API key?</summary>
      <p class="setup-manual-hint">
        Choose a provider and paste one of its API keys. We want to stress that your key is
        stored only in <strong>your browser</strong> (for details, see <a href="#api-key-safety">API key safety</a>).
        For OpenRouter, create a key at
        <a href="https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener">openrouter.ai/settings/keys</a>;
        if OpenRouter already showed you a key during sign-up, you can paste that one.
      </p>
      <label class="setup-field">
        <span>Provider</span>
        <select id="sg-provider">
          <option value="openrouter">OpenRouter</option>
          <option value="anthropic">Claude (Anthropic)</option>
          <option value="openai">OpenAI</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="setup-field" id="sg-row-anthropic" hidden>
        <span>Claude model</span>
        <select id="sg-anthropic-model">
          <option value="claude-haiku-4-5">Haiku 4.5 · fast &amp; cheap</option>
          <option value="claude-sonnet-5">Sonnet 5 · balanced</option>
          <option value="claude-opus-4-8">Opus 4.8 · most capable</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="setup-field" id="sg-row-openai" hidden>
        <span>OpenAI model</span>
        <select id="sg-openai-model">
          <option value="gpt-5.4-nano">GPT-5.4 nano · fast &amp; cheap</option>
          <option value="gpt-5.4-mini">GPT-5.4 mini · balanced</option>
          <option value="gpt-5.5">GPT-5.5 · most capable</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="setup-field">
        <span>API key</span>
        <input id="sg-key" type="password" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder="sk-or-…" />
      </label>
      <button id="sg-save" type="button">Save &amp; activate</button>
      <p>
      </p>
      <p class="setup-manual-hint">
        The OpenRouter option uses the free model selected above; for other providers you
        pick the model here. You can change any of this later in the assistant's ⚙ settings
        on chapter pages.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <p class="setup-note">
    We recommend <strong>NVIDIA Nemotron Nano 3 30B A3B</strong> as the default model.
    In our experience it offers generous free usage
    limits, although you are free to choose any compatible model.
  </p>

  <p class="setup-note">
    <strong>Note.</strong> Free models are shared by many users and are therefore subject
    to provider-imposed rate limits. During busy periods you may occasionally need to wait
    before sending another request or temporarily switch to a different model. If you
    expect to use the assistant extensively, you can also configure it with a paid API key
    from your preferred provider.
  </p>

  <aside class="callout security-note" id="api-key-safety">
    <h3 class="callout-label">API key safety</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Your API keys are stored only in your browser</strong> and used only to call the
      model provider you choose, directly from your device. <strong>We cannot receive, store, or
      log them.</strong>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>No account required on this site, and no server-side storage of any kind.</li>
      <li>
        Following our setup guide and connecting with OpenRouter never shows you a key at all: it creates one
        scoped to this site that you can inspect, cap, or revoke from your provider
        dashboard at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        Bringing your own Claude or OpenAI key? For extra safety, create a separate key
        with a small spending limit, and rotate or delete it any time from your provider
        dashboard.
      </li>
      <li>
        To see for yourself how we handle your API keys, inspect the
        <a href="https://github.com/pora-book/pora-book.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source code
        on GitHub</a> and watch
        exactly where requests go.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </aside>
</section>

<script>
  import {
    type Provider,
    loadSettings, saveSettings, isConfigured, fetchOpenRouterFreeModels,
    startOpenRouterConnect, completeOpenRouterConnect,
  } from '../scripts/assistant-config';

  type ManualProvider = Exclude<Provider, 'local'>;
  const KEY_PLACEHOLDERS: Record<ManualProvider, string> = {
    openrouter: 'sk-or-…',
    anthropic: 'sk-ant-…',
    openai: 'sk-…',
  };

  const modelSel = document.getElementById('sg-model') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
  const keyInput = document.getElementById('sg-key') as HTMLInputElement | null;
  const saveBtn = document.getElementById('sg-save') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
  const connectBtn = document.getElementById('sg-connect') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('sg-status');
  const providerSel = document.getElementById('sg-provider') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
  const anthropicRow = document.getElementById('sg-row-anthropic');
  const anthropicSel = document.getElementById('sg-anthropic-model') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
  const openaiRow = document.getElementById('sg-row-openai');
  const openaiSel = document.getElementById('sg-openai-model') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
  if (
    modelSel && keyInput && saveBtn && connectBtn && statusEl &&
    providerSel && anthropicRow && anthropicSel && openaiRow && openaiSel
  ) {
    const settings = loadSettings();
    if (settings.provider !== 'local') providerSel.value = settings.provider;
    anthropicSel.value = settings.anthropicModel;
    openaiSel.value = settings.openaiModel;
    // A model saved by an older version may no longer be in the list.
    if (openaiSel.value !== settings.openaiModel) openaiSel.selectedIndex = 0;
    if (isConfigured(settings)) {
      statusEl.textContent = '✓ Already set up — open any chapter and use the Ask button.';
    }

    // Show only the fields relevant to the chosen manual provider, and prefill
    // the key field with whatever the reader saved for it earlier.
    function reflectManual() {
      const p = providerSel!.value as ManualProvider;
      anthropicRow!.hidden = p !== 'anthropic';
      openaiRow!.hidden = p !== 'openai';
      keyInput!.placeholder = KEY_PLACEHOLDERS[p];
      keyInput!.value = loadSettings().keys[p] || '';
    }
    reflectManual();
    providerSel.addEventListener('change', reflectManual);

    // Returning from the openrouter.ai approval page with ?code=…
    completeOpenRouterConnect()
      .then((connected) => {
        if (!connected) return;
        providerSel.value = 'openrouter';
        reflectManual();
        statusEl.textContent =
          '✓ Connected to OpenRouter. Open any chapter and click the Ask button to start.';
        document.getElementById('assistant')?.scrollIntoView();
      })
      .catch((err) => {
        statusEl.textContent = `⚠️ ${err?.message || 'Connecting to OpenRouter failed. Please try again.'}`;
      });

    fetchOpenRouterFreeModels().then((models) => {
      modelSel.innerHTML = '';
      const list = models.length
        ? models
        : [{ id: settings.openrouterModel, name: settings.openrouterModel }];
      for (const m of list) {
        const opt = document.createElement('option');
        opt.value = m.id;
        opt.textContent = m.name.replace(/\s*\(free\)$/i, '') + ' · free';
        modelSel.appendChild(opt);
      }
      if (list.some((m) => m.id === settings.openrouterModel)) modelSel.value = settings.openrouterModel;
    });

    // Coming back from openrouter.ai via the back button restores the page from
    // the bfcache with the button still disabled — reset it.
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', (e) => {
      if (!(e as PageTransitionEvent).persisted) return;
      connectBtn.disabled = false;
      if (statusEl.textContent?.startsWith('Taking you')) statusEl.textContent = '';
    });

    connectBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      // Persist the chosen model now — it must survive the redirect round-trip.
      const s = loadSettings();
      if (modelSel.value) s.openrouterModel = modelSel.value;
      saveSettings(s);
      connectBtn.disabled = true;
      statusEl.textContent = 'Taking you to openrouter.ai…';
      startOpenRouterConnect();
    });

    saveBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const p = providerSel.value as ManualProvider;
      const key = keyInput.value.trim();
      if (!key) {
        statusEl.textContent = 'Paste your API key first.';
        return;
      }
      const s = loadSettings();
      s.provider = p;
      s.keys[p] = key;
      if (p === 'openrouter' && modelSel.value) s.openrouterModel = modelSel.value;
      if (p === 'anthropic') s.anthropicModel = anthropicSel.value;
      if (p === 'openai') s.openaiModel = openaiSel.value;
      saveSettings(s);
      statusEl.textContent = '✓ Saved. Open any chapter and click the Ask button to start.';
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .home-assistant { margin-top: 3.5rem; }
  .setup-steps { margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .home-assistant code {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05); padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .setup-form {
    display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; max-width: 32rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule, #e6ddcd); border-radius: 12px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent, #c65a3a) 4%, var(--paper, #fff));
  }
  .setup-field { display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .setup-field > span { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .setup-field select, .setup-field input {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule, #e6ddcd);
    border-radius: 8px; background: #fff; color: var(--ink, #24211d); font: inherit;
  }
  #sg-save, #sg-connect {
    justify-self: start; border: none; border-radius: 9px; background: var(--accent, #c65a3a);
    color: #fff; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
  #sg-save:hover, #sg-connect:hover { filter: brightness(1.05); }
  #sg-connect:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; }
  .setup-status { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; min-height: 1.2em; color: var(--ink-soft, #6b6459); }
  .setup-manual { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule, #e6ddcd); padding-top: 0.6rem; }
  .setup-manual summary {
    cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #6b6459);
  }
  .setup-manual[open] summary { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .setup-manual-hint { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .setup-manual .setup-field { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .setup-note { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.8; }
  /* Box chrome comes from the shared .callout in global.css. */
  .security-note { margin-top: 2rem; scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem; }
</style>
